# Deliberately no rules. See the note below before adding any.
#
# The thermal HAL produces these denials:
#
#   avc: denied { add_name write } scontext=u:r:hal_thermal_default:s0
#        tcontext=u:object_r:sysfs_thermal:s0 tclass=dir
#   avc: denied { create } name="trip_point_1_temp" ... tclass=file
#
# Allowing them was tried on 2026-08-08 and the build rejected it:
#
#   system/sepolicy/private/domain.te:1576
#   neverallow domain sysfs_type:dir
#       { add_name create link remove_name rename reparent rmdir write };
#
# AOSP forbids this for *every* domain, with no exceptions, so the denial is
# meant to fail. The cause is benign probing: the device has 72 thermal zones
# and only 54 expose trip_point_1_temp. The HAL walks all of them, and
# fopen(path, "w") passes O_CREAT, so the 18 without that node look like
# creation attempts.
#
# Nothing is broken by this. The zones that have the node are written normally
# -- there has never been a `file write` denial, only `create`. If a real write
# is ever refused, that will show up as its own denial and can be granted then.
